    <!-- ViewModel / services -->
    <string name="auto_tune_vpn_running">Turn off VPN first — tuning needs the engine exclusively.</string>
    <string name="current_command">current command</string>
    <string name="auto_tune_none_worked">No method broke the block. Try manually in advanced settings.</string>
    <string name="auto_tune_engine_stuck">The bypass engine did not shut down and is still holding the device. Restart the app, then run auto-tune again.</string>
    <!-- Something else claimed the engine part-way through the sweep — enabling the VPN from the
         quick-settings tile is the usual way in. Nothing is broken and nothing was saved: every
         method from that point on was refused the engine rather than tested, so the results would
         have described our own process and not the network. Deliberately different advice from
         auto_tune_engine_stuck, which needs a restart; this one just needs the other thing off. -->
    <string name="auto_tune_engine_taken">Something else took the bypass engine mid-check, so the rest of the methods were never tested. Turn the VPN off and tune again.</string>
    <!-- Between the tap on «Stop tuning» and the sweep actually ending: the method under test owns
         the engine until it finishes, and a progress line frozen mid-count would read as a hang. -->
    <string name="auto_tune_cancelling">Stopping — waiting for the current check to finish…</string>
    <!-- Outcome of a stopped sweep. Says the method was left alone, because a sweep cut short has
         tested some strategies and applied none of them. -->
    <string name="auto_tune_cancelled">Tuning stopped — the method was left as it was.</string>
    <!-- Replaces the sweep entirely: with nothing resolvable there is nothing to test, and pointing
         the user at bypass methods would send them after the wrong problem. -->
    <string name="auto_tune_dns_failed">None of the sites resolve on this network — that\'s DNS, not a block, and no bypass method can fix it. Change the network\'s DNS or switch networks.</string>
