    <!-- The two stage keys are substituted as %1$s into vpn_fail_format, so they have to complete
         that sentence: a noun phrase after "Could not complete", an infinitive after "Не удалось". -->
    <string name="vpn_fail_start_stage">VPN start</string>
    <string name="vpn_fail_establish_stage">VPN establish</string>
    <string name="vpn_fail_format">Could not complete %1$s: %2$s: %3$s</string>
    <string name="vpn_fail_no_details">no details</string>
    <!-- byedpi's own main() answered -1, which on Android means init()/run() failed and the bind lost
         the port. The old wording hedged with "or engine already running" because the shim returned
         -1 for that too and the two could not be told apart; byedpi_engine_busy now covers it, so the
         hedge is gone and the advice can be acted on. -->
    <string name="byedpi_port_busy">byedpi failed to start — port %1$d is taken. Close ByeByeDPI/other SOCKS apps and try again</string>
    <!-- The start never happened: the single native engine was already claimed and the gate refused,
         without touching anything. No port to free and no command to fix, so neither is mentioned.
         Opens with "byedpi failed to start" like every sibling below — this lands in the same
         diagnostics line under the VPN card, where a message that renamed the subject to "the bypass
         engine" would read as a different subsystem reporting. -->
    <string name="byedpi_engine_busy">byedpi failed to start — the engine is already in use by another run. Wait for method tuning to finish, or restart the app if this keeps happening</string>
    <string name="byedpi_exit_code">byedpi exited immediately (code %1$d). Check the byedpi command in settings</string>
